The sequence has first term \(a=\frac14\) and common ratio \(r=\frac12\).

Sum of first \(n\) terms:
\[
S_n = a\frac{1-r^n}{1-r}
= \frac14\frac{1-(1/2)^n}{1-1/2}
= \frac12\left(1-\frac1{2^n}\right).
\]

Set equal to \(\frac{255}{512}\):
\[
\frac12\left(1-\frac1{2^n}\right)=\frac{255}{512}
\implies 1-\frac1{2^n}=\frac{255}{256}
\implies \frac1{2^n}=\frac1{256}
\implies 2^n=256.
\]

Thus \(n=8\).

\[
\boxed{8}
\]

